      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14222856/assets/4777b642ae90300bcdcb33e2377067113a78f04a5a891a1c332178619291b6ad.png)\n\nNancy is making lemonade. The amount of water she needs for a given amount of lemon juice is given in the graph above. In its simplest form, what is the ratio of lemon juice to water?",
      "worked_solution": "One of the points belonging to the graph is $(10,15).$\n\nLet's write the ratio $10:15$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{15}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this fraction by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10÷5}{15÷5} & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the ratio of lemon juice to water is $2:3.$",
